<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trajan's Column</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">113 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>'s Column is a Roman triumphal column in Trajan's Forum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, dedicated in 113 CE. Its spiral frieze, about 190 metres long, shows the emperor's two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajans-dacian-wars">Dacian Wars</a> of 101–102 and 105–106 CE in more than 2,500 figures and is a major source for the Roman army and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacians">Dacians</a>. Trajan's ashes were placed in its base.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trajans-column.jpg" alt="Trajan's Column" width="320" height="746" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Livioandronico2013 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trajan%27s_Column_HD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
